  "id": "COMPOUND:31725 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Kadsuralignan H appears to exert its biological effects through a series of interconnected targets, ultimately leading to a relationship with Phosphodiesterase 6C (PDE6C). The evidence suggests that Kadsuralignan H acts as a modulator of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including (16S)-21-methyl-18-oxa-1,11-diazahexacyclo[11.8.0.02,16.04,12.05,10.015,20]henicosa-4(12),5,7,9-tetraen-17-ol and 6'-O-Z-Para-Methoxycinnamoylharpagide. These compounds are all implicated in the regulation of PDE6C, suggesting a potential mechanism involving the inhibition or modulation of PDE6C activity. The consistent presence of these targets and their shared interaction with Kadsuralignan H indicates a plausible pathway where the drug may influence PDE6C through a series of intermediate steps, possibly involving enzymatic regulation or signaling pathways. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Kadsuralignan H and PDE6C, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
